# Life and Limb (turn 1), then Blood Moon (turn 5); both apply in layer 4 (CR 613.1d).
# - Taiga and Dryad Arbor are nonbasic Forests. Applying Blood Moon makes them Mountains and not Forests, which changes
#   what Life and Limb applies to, so Life and Limb's effect depends on Blood Moon's (CR 613.8a) and waits until after it
#   (CR 613.8b), though it is older. Applying Life and Limb changes nothing Blood Moon applies to - every Forest and Saproling
#   here is a land already - so Blood Moon does not depend on it. After the Moon neither land is a Forest or a Saproling, so
#   Life and Limb does not apply to them at all: Taiga is a plain Land - Mountain, no creature, tapping for {R}; Dryad Arbor
#   is a Land Creature - Dryad Mountain, 1/1 and green by its own card, and no Saproling. (Applied in timestamp order, Life
#   and Limb would first make them Saprolings, and they would stay Saproling creatures under the Moon.) Before the Moon both
#   are 1/1 green Saproling Forests. With a Saproling that is no land on the battlefield, the two depend on each other
#   (blood-moon-and-life-and-limb-made-to-depend-on-each-other-by-a-woodland-changeling-apply-in-timestamp-order).

[Bot1 Deck]
Taiga
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Life and Limb
Dryad Arbor
Blood Moon
Plains
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x30

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Taiga.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Life and Limb.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Taiga.Activate(Ability: Add {G})
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Taiga.Subtypes = Forest; Mountain; Saproling
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Dryad Arbor.Play
? Bot1.Battlefield.Dryad Arbor.Subtypes = Dryad; Forest; Saproling
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Blood Moon.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Taiga.Subtypes = Mountain
! Bot1.Battlefield.Taiga.Activate(Ability: Add {G})
Bot1.Battlefield.Taiga.Activate(Ability: Add {R})
? Bot1.Mana = {R}

[Expect]
Turn = 5
Bot1.Battlefield.Taiga.Types = Land
Bot1.Battlefield.Taiga.Subtypes = Mountain
Bot1.Battlefield.Taiga.Colors = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Dryad Arbor.Types = Land; Creature
Bot1.Battlefield.Dryad Arbor.Subtypes = Dryad; Mountain
Bot1.Battlefield.Dryad Arbor.Colors = Green
Bot1.Battlefield.Dryad Arbor.Power = 1
